  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 929 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nThe center of the ridge will begin to gradually flatten through\nthe week, but Major (Level 3/4) heat impacts will continue\nthrough the work week. This is due to highs in the mid 90s and \ndewpoints in the mid to upper 70s creating heat index values in \nexcess of 105 degrees each day. In addition to the heat, low \nchances (20-30%) of diurnally driven showers and thunderstorms \nwill return to the forecast each afternoon Tuesday through Friday,\nthanks to the deep moisture in place. The one caveat would be if \nthe ridge shifts a little further to the west, placing the area \nunder northwest flow aloft. Should this play out, we may be more \nunder the threat for MCS activity that rides along the edge of the\nridge. We'll have to watch this in the days to come. Overall, hot\nand humid weather for the foreseeable future.",
